---
epr-meta-version: 1
id: ark-envelope-declaration
covers: subtree
purpose: >
  The ark compute-envelope crate family declares runtime resources in pure core;
  the supervisor owns effects and the CLI owns invocation.
rules:
  - id: declaration-is-not-enforcement
    class: inject
    when:
      write: "*.rs"
      contains-any: ["RuntimeEnvelope", "ResourceQuota", "ProcessQuota", "memory_bound"]
    dedupe-of: "elohim/ark/CLAUDE.md (Declared S0 simplifications) + elohim/ark/core/src/passport.rs (EffectiveTier)"
    why: >
      A manifest field never implies enforcement. Envelope limits, protected children,
      shed order and graded obligations are declarations only; EffectiveTier stays None
      until a later runtime implements and witnesses enforcement. Reuse epr-rea Bound
      and Composition for projection; never mint a parallel bound ontology.
---

# ark — envelope declaration

The two Station 1 decisions are registered in seam-registry.yaml. Reciprocity
ledger events belong to the future enforcing runtime, not the manifest declaration.

`covers: subtree` claims all three crates: `core/` (pure data and decisions),
`supervisor/` (I/O, no network) and `cli/` (the `ark` binary). The purity boundary is
structural rather than edit-time. `boundary::no_runtime_or_io_deps` refuses runtime and
I/O dependencies in ark-core's own `Cargo.toml`, and `boundary::no_fs_in_pure_core`
refuses filesystem access in its sources, so a violation fails the crate's tests.
